  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure builds into the Ohio Valley from the southeast today \nbringing dry and mostly clear conditions. Forecast highs reach into \nthe lower 60s to upper 50s. Tuesday and Wednesday will also feature \nmoderating temperatures with highs in the 60s. Cloud cover starts to \nincrease on Wednesday ahead of an approaching low pressure system. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nA low pressure system moves through the Lower Great Lakes or Ohio \nValley on Thursday. There is a descent amount of model spread \nregarding the strength and path of the low. In general, increasing \nclouds develop Wednesday night into Thursday morning along with rain \nmoving in from west to east. Once the low progresses east of the \narea on Thursday, much cooler temperatures on breezy northerly flow \ncan be expected. Any lingering wrap around precipitation could start \nfeaturing a few wet snow flakes by Friday. Precipitation chances \nlikely end by Friday night. Cool conditions and breezy northerly \nflow persists through the first part of the weekend.",
